{1 Disassembler}


The disassembler is, in some sense, an inverse of the assembler. It takes [Gaur ISA] binaries as input and generates the corresponding [Gaur ASM] assembly files. However, the assembly files generated lack labels and pseudo-instructions (for now).

{2 Web tool}

The web version of disassembler can be found {{:../tools/disassembler.html} here}

{2 Usage}

The [dis] executable can be invoked with various flags. To see an exhaustive list of the same, invoke it with the [--help] flag. The output will be something like this:

{v
λ⟩ dis --help
Usage: dis [options] <input_file_path>.
  --out 
        Path for the generated Gaur ASM output
  -o 
        Short for --out
  --help 
        Display this list of options
  -help 
        Display this list of options
  -h 
        Short for --help / -help
v}


{2 Example}

Assume that [fib.gin] is the binary file corresponding to the [fib.gsm] program from [assembler/examples], generated using [assembler] with the [-fmt=bin] flag.

It can be disassembled as follows:

{v
λ⟩ dis fib.gin -o fib-disassembled.gsm
Wrote: fib-disassembled.gsm

λ⟩ cat fib-disassembled.gsm 
ld r1 r0 0
ld r2 r0 1
addi r3 r0 0
addi r5 r0 0
addi r6 r0 1
beq r3 r1 7
add r4 r2 r3
st r5 r4 0
add r6 r6 r5
sub r5 r6 r5
addi r3 r3 1
j -6
j 0
v}


{2 Source code and documentation}

The source code for the assembler can be found on our {{:https://gitlab.com/verify-at-iitpkd/gaur/} GitLab repository}, in the [disassembler] directory.

The [odoc] generated documentation for the libraries involved can be read here:

- {!Dis.Errors}: The errors that can be thrown by the disassembler.
- {!Dis.Decode}: Functions to decode [Gaur ISA] instructions and programs.

{b {i NOTE:}} The disassembler makes use of types and printers defined in the assembler.

